ADF: 0.1

📋 CONTEXT [advisory]:
  - Content-only docs repo. Every session involves reading, summarizing, or writing doc pages.
  - Pages live in src/content/docs/<slug>.md — Astro Content Collection with glob() loader.
  - Schema is Zod-typed in src/content.config.ts. Sidebar order, prev/next, and search auto-derive from frontmatter.

⚠ CONSTRAINTS [load-bearing]:
  - Every doc page requires this frontmatter:
      title: "Page Title"   # sidebar, breadcrumb, search
      section: "charter"    # charter | platform | ecosystem
      order: 7              # numeric — controls sidebar + prev/next ordering
      color: "#hexcode"     # hex; derive from SECTION_META in src/lib/navigation.ts
      tag: "07"             # zero-padded string of `order`
    Optional: description, lastVerified, sourceSlug.
  - Section colors are canonical in SECTION_META in src/lib/navigation.ts. Always derive from there — never guess or hardcode from memory.
  - Changing frontmatter keys or the Zod schema in src/content.config.ts requires checking src/lib/navigation.ts for downstream consumers.

🔌 SKILLS [load-bearing]:
  - aegis-delegate — before reading any doc page for exploration or summary, check line count:
        wc -l src/content/docs/<slug>.md
      If >300 lines → delegate first:
        node ~/.claude/skills/aegis-delegate/delegate.js [provider] summarize <path> "what you need"
      Read directly only when: (a) about to edit (Edit tool needs exact line numbers), (b) verbatim text required.
  - /docs skill — for multi-page audits, stale content detection, or GitHub issue sync:
        /docs              # full sweep + commit
        /docs --no-issues  # content-only, skip GitHub
        /docs --no-commit  # dry-run, report only
    Invoke via Skill tool when doing cross-page documentation maintenance.

📖 GUIDE [advisory]:
  - Understanding a page → check LOC → delegate if >300, else Read.
  - Editing a page → Read directly (need exact line numbers for Edit tool).
  - Cross-page audit or stale sweep → /docs skill.
  - Adding a page: create src/content/docs/<slug>.md with required frontmatter; derive color from SECTION_META; page auto-appears in sidebar, search, and prev/next.
